  "id": "r3-per-call-ops",
  "title": "Per-Call Operations",
  "description": "An agent holds an auth token where list_calendar_events is granted outright and create_calendar_event is r3_per_call — authorized in principle, but not for any specific call. When the agent invokes it, the resource builds a per-call proposal: a full R3 document scoped to that one invocation, carrying the call's concrete parameters. The resource token references it by r3_uri and r3_s256 only, so the parameters never travel in a token. The AS evaluates those parameters, and the resource verifies the actual call against the approved proposal before serving it.",
  "spec_section": "§ Per-Call Proposals",
