      "annotations": [
        "The agent presents its auth token and invokes create_calendar_event. The resource matches it in r3_per_call, not r3_granted.",
        "An r3_per_call operation is authorized in principle but not for any specific call: the consequences depend on the concrete parameters — who is invited, how large the payment is, which record is deleted.",
        "The resource builds a per-call proposal — a full R3 document scoped to this one invocation, with the same structure, the same content-addressing and the same AS/PS-only fetch restriction as a class document. -02 made these full R3 documents rather than a bespoke shape.",
        "It persists the proposal keyed by its r3_s256 and returns a resource token whose r3_uri and r3_s256 reference it. The token carries only the reference — never the parameters. That keeps tokens small and binds the eventual approval to the exact call proposed.",
        "The agenda parameter is represented as a digest with a short excerpt: large or sensitive values stay out of every token and away from the PS. The full bytes travel from the agent to the resource at call time."
      ],
